    "body": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42121 broke \"-L\" and \"-l\" for commits specific to 1 file\r\nbecause majority of Vim commits are tagged\r\nand \"git log --tags --no-walk\" is inconsistent for 1-file queries. \"git log --stdin --no-walk\" does work so it's always required regardless of additional formatting.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nTags v9.0.0055 and v9.0.0056 are on the same commit. Detecting 1 of the tags resolves the other for \"-L\" and \"-l\". Patch 9.0.0056 is N/A based on\r\ncommit e15f79c659f8895afdb946333757ad5517329805 .\r\nvim-patch.sh can't auto-detect v9.0.0056 yet.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nTODO\r\nPrevent developer from overwriting essential \"--format=\" flags else vim-patch.sh produces invalid Git refs.\r\n\r\n/cc @zeertzjq to review",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-04T03:28:46Z",
    "comment_data": [
